package planner

const caseContractInstructions = `CASE CONTRACTS
In Pass B, formalize evidence-backed code obligations in done.args.case_invariants (an array), or in an investigation's case_invariants array. Each entry describes what should hold, never an assessment that it is already satisfied or violated.
Shape:
{"lead_ref":"<lead_id opened in this sample>","subjects":[{"path":"relative/source.c","symbol":"actual_function"}],"preconditions":["explicit condition under which the obligation applies"],"required_property":{"kind":"specific property kind","statement":"the precise obligation","source":"optional value producer","destination":"optional consumer or field","authority":"optional decision point","target_fields":[]},"security_effect":"the decision affected","evidence_refs":[{"kind":"source","path":"relative/source.c","symbol":"actual_function","start_line":1,"end_line":5}],"verification_queries":[],"related_twes":[]}
Use only source ranges and symbols you read. lead_ref must name this sample's real AuditLead and its target must occur among subjects. Use verification_queries.parameters.subject="path::symbol" to identify the function being verified whenever the contract has multiple subjects; its order alone does not identify the query target. If preconditions or the security effect depend on a consumer/caller such as the function that checks a version, include its observed definition as an additional subject; do not invent a consumer location. Scope, hashes and source binding are checked by the program. Do not fabricate those values. If the obligation cannot be grounded, keep the lead and explain the missing evidence instead of claiming completion. related_twes may be empty.
Registered verification initially supports only a narrow local property: kind="direct_struct_field_assignment", a primary subject function (additional consumer subjects provide context), destination="StructName.field", target_fields=["field"], no source value, and verification_queries=[{"backend":"codeql","operation":"cpp.contract.direct_struct_field_assignment","parameters":{"type":"StructName","field":"field","subject":"relative/source.c::actual_function"}}]. Its statement must mean only that this exact function definition contains a direct Assignment AST node to that struct field. Initializers, helper calls, indirect writes and overloaded assignments do not satisfy this syntactic property; compound assignment nodes do. This does not prove source-value propagation, output aliasing, control-flow dominance, or all-path correctness. For stronger or other properties use the accurate kind and leave verification_queries empty; the missing verification method remains explicit. Do not weaken a security obligation merely to fit the registered query.

`
